<article class="env-lemma" id="008X">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/008X">Lemma <span data-tag="008X">6.24.6</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a continuous map of topological spaces. Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a sheaf of rings on $Y$. Let $\mathcal{G}$ be a sheaf of $\mathcal{O}$-modules. There is a natural map of underlying presheaves of sets </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  f^{-1}\mathcal{O} \times f^{-1}\mathcal{G} \longrightarrow f^{-1}\mathcal{G}  \]
</div>
  <p> which turns $f^{-1}\mathcal{G}$ into a sheaf of $f^{-1}\mathcal{O}$-modules. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Recall that $f^{-1}$ is defined as the composition of the functor $f_ p$ and sheafification. Thus the lemma is a combination of Lemma <a href="/tag/008T" data-tag="008T">6.24.2</a> and Lemma <a href="/tag/0089" data-tag="0089">6.20.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>